            <div xml:id="d518">

                <pb facs="0593" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg581"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00118 European War 1939/735a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Leopoldville</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Mallon</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-23T23:00:00-05:00">October 23,
                            1941—11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Colonel Cunningham from General Miles. You should avoid any publicity,
                    particularly press interviews. Your duty is strictly confined to fact finding
                    and you head no mission. Brazzaville Sedgewick despatch which appeared in Oct.
                    16 <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi> is called to your attention.
                    [Miles.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
